<li>
<p><strong>Sol. c.</strong>
    The unit digits of perfect squares can only be 0, 1, 4, 5, 6, 9.
    Digits 2, 3, 7, 8 cannot be the unit digit of a perfect square.
    Therefore, 7 cannot be a unit digit of a perfect square.</p>
</li>
<li>
